We conclude that, on balance, there is greater 
evidence to support the parsimonious hypothesis 
that this was a patient with an unusually long course 
of encephalomyelitis whose presenting clinical fea- 
tures resembled those of SPS. 
Video, polygraphic (32), and pathologic studies in 
additional patients with these conditions may deter- 
mine the significance and specificity of the unique 
polygraphic and pathologic findings in our patient. 
